    "body": "I'm not aware such issues, but also that doesn't tell anything about this case, assuming I understand the proposal that there would be two input events. One for the unchecked and one for the checked radio button.\r\nConceptually firing input on unchecked radio button, which itself didn't get any input, sounds a bit wrong.",
