    "created_at": "2017-03-24T15:03:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-03-24T15:03:21Z",
    "body": "I think what smaug is saying is that it doesn't make sense to fire an input event on an element that hasn't itself received input. However, if you instead think of it as \"there was an input somewhere, and the value of this element was changed because of it\", it does make some sense. The real problem is that radio buttons just don't act like any other input type, because when they're grouped together they act like a single element.",
